# --- Data providers -----------------------------------------------------
# All of these default to "live" — real data via keyless public APIs
# (Yahoo Finance for market data/news, Frankfurter/ECB for FX, World Bank
# for macro indicators), with an automatic, transparent fallback to
# mock/sample data if the live call fails for any reason (network down,
# rate limited, unsupported symbol/region). No API key or signup needed
# for any of it. Override to force a specific mode:
#   MARKET_DATA_PROVIDER=mock       pure mock, never touches the network
#   MARKET_DATA_PROVIDER=yahoo      pure live, no fallback (fails loudly)
#   MARKET_DATA_PROVIDER=live       live with mock fallback (default)
# Same pattern for NEWS_PROVIDER (mock/yahoo/live), FX_RATE_PROVIDER
# (mock/frankfurter/live), and MACRO_PROVIDER (mock/worldbank/live).
# See src/lib/*/providers/index.ts to add another real source.
MARKET_DATA_PROVIDER=live
NEWS_PROVIDER=live
MACRO_PROVIDER=live
FX_RATE_PROVIDER=live

# --- Quant service --------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of apps/quant-api. The Next.js API routes proxy to this.
QUANT_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# --- Auth (Clerk) ----------------------------------------------------------
# Optional for now. Leave both unset and the app runs unauthenticated with
# mock data (a fixed "demo-user" owns the sample portfolio). Set both to
# enable real sign-in — get keys from https://dashboard.clerk.com.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=

# --- Portfolio & watchlist storage ------------------------------------------
# PORTFOLIO_STORAGE=sqlite (default) persists holdings to a local SQLite
# file via Node's built-in node:sqlite — no external database service, no
# signup, no paid tier. Set PORTFOLIO_STORAGE=mock to force the old
# in-memory-only behavior (resets on every restart). If SQLite fails to
# initialize (e.g. no write access to DATABASE_PATH), the app
# automatically falls back to in-memory storage for that run and logs a
# warning — it never hard-fails on this.
# PORTFOLIO_STORAGE=sqlite
#
# WATCHLIST_STORAGE=sqlite (default) does the same for the tracked-symbols
# list on the Markets/Overview pages — same options (sqlite/mock), same
# automatic fallback behavior, independent of PORTFOLIO_STORAGE.
# WATCHLIST_STORAGE=sqlite
#
# Where the SQLite file lives. Defaults to ./.data/app.db (relative to the
# process's working directory), created automatically if missing. Shared
# by both portfolio and watchlist storage.
# DATABASE_PATH=./.data/app.db
